# 7. Docker Hub
Docker Hub ek cloud-based container registry hai jahan Docker Images ko store, manage aur share kiya jata hai. Ye Docker ka official repository platform hai. Jab bhi hume koi ready-made image (jaise Nginx, Ubuntu, MySQL, Node.js) chahiye hoti hai, hum Docker Hub se download kar sakte hain.

> Why Docker Hub is Used?
Images ko store karne ke liye
Images ko share karne ke liye
Team collaboration ke liye
Application deployment ko easy banane ke liye
Public aur private image management ke liye

# What is Public Repository?
Public Repository ek aisi repository hoti hai jise internet par koi bhi user access aur download kar sakta hai.
> Use:
Open-source projects share karne ke liye
Community ke saath images distribute karne ke liye
Common software images provide karne ke liye
> Example:
Ubuntu
Nginx
Redis
MySQL

# What is Private Repository?
Private Repository ek secure repository hoti hai jise sirf authorized users hi access kar sakte hain.

> Use:
Company projects ke liye
Sensitive applications ke liye
Internal software distribution ke liye
Security maintain karne ke liye

# Login to Docker Hub

Docker Hub account ko local Docker environment se connect karne ki process ko login kehte hain.

Use:
Images push karne ke liye
Private repositories access karne ke liye
User authentication ke liye


# Pull Images
Docker Hub se image download karne ki process ko pull kehte hain.

Use:
Ready-made images use karne ke liye
Application deployment fast karne ke liye
Time aur effort bachane ke liye

Example:
Ubuntu image download karna.

# Push Images
Local system me bani image ko Docker Hub par upload karne ki process ko push kehte hain.

Use:
Team members ke saath image share karne ke liye
CI/CD pipelines me deployment ke liye
Backup aur version management ke liye

# Publish Image
Jab image successfully Docker Hub par upload ho jati hai aur dusre users ke liye available ho jati hai, ise image publish karna kehte hain.

Use:
Software distribution
Deployment automation
Public sharing
Collaboration


🟠 8. Docker Compose
Docker Compose ek tool hai jo multiple containers ko ek saath manage aur run karne ke liye use hota hai.

Real-world applications me sirf ek container nahi hota. Ek application ke liye frontend, backend, database, cache etc. alag-alag containers hote hain. Docker Compose in sabko ek hi configuration file se manage karta hai.

Why Docker Compose is Used?
Multi-container applications run karne ke liye
Configuration simplify karne ke liye
Development environment setup fast karne ke liye
Multiple services ko ek command se start/stop karne ke liye

# docker-compose.yml Syntax
Docker Compose ki configuration ek YAML file me likhi jati hai jise docker-compose.yml kehte hain.

> Is file me define kiya jata hai:
Kaunsi services run hongi
Kaunsi image use hogi
Kaunsa port expose hoga
Volumes aur networks kya honge
Environment variables kya honge

> Use:
Application infrastructure ko code ke form me define karne ke liye.

# Multi-container Applications
Aisi applications jisme multiple services milkar kaam karti hain unhe multi-container applications kehte hain.

> Example:
React Frontend
Node.js Backend
MongoDB Database

Ye tino alag containers me run ho sakte hain aur ek dusre se communicate karte hain.

> Use:
Microservices architecture
Scalable applications
Better isolation and management

# docker-compose up
Ye command docker-compose.yml file me defined sabhi services ko create aur start karti hai.

Use:
Puri application ko start karne ke liye
Development environment launch karne ke liye
Multiple containers ek saath run karne ke liye

# docker-compose down
Ye command running services, containers aur networks ko stop aur remove karti hai.

Use:
Environment cleanup ke liye
Resource release karne ke liye
Application shutdown ke liye

# Service Configuration
Service Configuration ka matlab hai har service ke settings define karna.

Isme define kiya jata hai:

Image
Container Name
Ports
Volumes
Networks
Environment Variables
Dependencies
Use:
Consistent environment create karne ke liye
Service communication manage karne ke liye
Infrastructure automation ke liye



Q: What is Docker Hub?
A: Docker Hub is a cloud-based registry used to store, manage, and distribute Docker images.

Q: What is the difference between Public and Private Repositories?
A: Public repositories are accessible to everyone, while private repositories are accessible only to authorized users.

Q: Why do we use Docker Compose?
A: Docker Compose is used to manage and run multiple containers using a single configuration file.

Q: What is a Multi-container Application?
A: An application that consists of multiple services running in separate containers.

